s might interact and what insights they could provide about fiscal performance.\n\nWhen examining the third span from July 1964 to January 1965, I'm seeing another set of monthly figures that suggest ongoing financial tracking. I'll carefully calculate the ranges and percentages to understand the financial dynamics across these periods.\n\nI'll verify the totals and percentages, focusing on precise calculations to ensure accuracy in the financial analysis.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_f2fd278fb57240f8","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Data from the Treasury Bulletin pages\n# FY 1962-63 (July 1962 - January 1963)\nfy62_63 = [5528, 4637, 4770, 7342, 3841, 5374, 4206]\n\n# FY 1963-64 (July 1963 - January 1964)\nfy63_64 = [6730, 5350, 5765, 6813, 4022, 4792, 4995]\n\n# FY 1964-65 (July 1964 - January 1965)\nfy64_65 = [6519, 4514, 4880, 6434, 3394, 6699, 4198]\n\n# Calculate 3-month spans\n# First span: months 0-2 (July, August, September)\n# Second span: months 2-4 (September, October, November) - overlapping? \n# Or maybe non-overlapping: months 0-2, 3-5, 5-6? \n\n# Let me check what makes sense - \"3 spans\" for 7 months - likely non-overlapping 3-month periods\n# Actually, let me interpret this as: consecutive 3-month periods within July-January\n\n# The problem says \"each 3 spans\" - probably means three 3-month periods within each fiscal year\n# For July-January (7 months), we can form: \n# - months 0-2 (Jul-Aug-Sep), months 2-4 (Sep-Oct-Nov), months 4-6 (Nov-Dec-Jan)\n# OR non-overlapping: Jul-Aug-Sep, Oct-Nov-Dec, Jan (but only 1 month left)\n\n# Let me assume overlapping 3-month periods starting at each month\n# So for 7 months: months 0-2, 1-3, 2-4, 3-5, 4-6 (5 periods per year)\n\n# Actually wait - re-reading: \"compute the range of the balance present for each 3 spans\"\n# This could mean 3 different fiscal year spans (FY62-63, FY63-64, FY64-65)\n# And we need to look at