t span from July to January. I need to analyze the range and average balance across these three spans systematically.\n\nI'll calculate the range by finding the difference between maximum and minimum balances for each fiscal year. Then I'll determine the percentage range by dividing the range by the average balance and multiplying by 100. This approach will help me compare the variability across these three fiscal years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_32bda1a19591dc1a","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Alternate interpretation: The 3 spans are the 3 fiscal years themselves\n# We compute range across all July-January months in each fiscal year\n\n# FY 1962-63 (July 1962 - January 1963)\nfy62_63 = [5528, 4637, 4770, 7342, 3841, 5374, 4206]\n\n# FY 1963-64 (July 1963 - January 1964)\nfy63_64 = [6730, 5350, 5765, 6813, 4022, 4792, 4995]\n\n# FY 1964-65 (July 1964 - January 1965)\nfy64_65 = [6519, 4514, 4880, 6434, 3394, 6699, 4198]\n\nimport statistics\n\ndef calc_range_pct(balances, label):\n    min_b = min(balances)\n    max_b = max(balances)\n    range_val = max_b - min_b\n    avg = statistics.mean(balances)\n    pct = (range_val / avg) * 100\n    print(f\"{label}: Range = {range_val}, Avg = {avg:.2f}, % = {pct:.2f}\")\n    return pct\n\nprint(\"=== Interpretation 1: Full July-January period for each FY ===\")\npct1 = calc_range_pct(fy62_63, \"FY 1962-63\")\npct2 = calc_range_pct(fy63_64, \"FY 1963-64\")\npct3 = calc_range_pct(fy64_65, \"FY 1964-65\")\n\nall_pcts = [pct1, pct2, pct3]\nprint(f\"All percentages: {all_pcts}\")\nprint(f\"Highest: {max(all_pcts):.2f}\")\n\n# Alternate interpretation 2: 3 non-overlapping 3-month periods\n# For each fiscal year: Jul-Sep, Oct-Dec, Jan (but Jan is only 1 month...)\n# Actually let's try Jul-Aug-Sep, Oct-Nov-Dec, and... \n# Or maybe it's: Jul-Sep, Aug-Oct-Nov, Sep-Nov-Dec (overlapping)\n\n# Interpretation 3: Just 3 months in each span (like first 3 months)\nprint(\"\\n=== Interpretation 2: First 3 months only (Jul-Sep) ===\")\npct1 = calc_range_pct(fy62_63[:3], \"FY 1962-63 Jul-Sep\")\npct2 = calc_range_pct(fy63_64[:3], \"FY 1963-64 Jul-Sep\")\npct3 = calc_range_pct(fy64_65[:3], \"FY 1964-65 Jul-Sep\")\n\nall_pcts = [pct1, pct2, pct3]\nprint(f\"All percentages: {all_pcts}\")\nprint(f\"Highest: {max(all_pcts):.2f}\")\n\n# Hmm, this doesn't seem right either\n# Let me think more... \n\n# Interpretation 4: Perhaps the \"3 spans\" means:\n# - fiscal year 1962-63\n# - fiscal year 1963-64  \n# - fiscal year 1964-65\n\n# But we need 3 spans within each... wait, maybe it's about comparing across the 3 years?\n# No, the problem specifically asks about \"each 3 spans\"\n\n# Let me try another approach - maybe \"3 spans\" means we divide July-January (7 months)\n# into 3 roughly equal periods:\n# - Period 1: Jul, Aug, Sep (months 0,1,2) \n# - Period 2: Sep, Oct, Nov (months 2,3,4) - overlapping\n# - Period 3: Nov, Dec, Jan (months 4,5,6) - overlapping\n\n# That would give us 3 spans per fiscal year\n\nprint(\"\\n=== Interpretation 3: Three 3-month spans per FY (overlapping) ===\")\nfor year_name, balances in [(\"FY 1962-63\", fy62_63), (\"FY 1963-64\", fy63_64), (\"FY 1964-65\", fy64_65)]:\n    print(f\"\\n{year_name}:\")\n    # Span 1: months 0,1,2 (Jul, Aug, Sep)\n    span1 = [balances[0], balances[1], balances[2]]\n    # Span 2: months 2,3,4 (Sep, Oct, Nov)\n    span2 = [balances[2], balances[3], balances[4]]\n    # Span 3: months 4,5,6 (Nov, Dec, Jan)\n    span3 = [balances[4], balances[5], balances[6]]\n    \n    pct1 = calc_range_pct(span1, f\"  Span 1 (Jul-Sep): {span1}\")\n    pct2 = calc_range_pct(span2, f\"  Span 2 (Sep-Nov): {span2}\")\n    pct3 = calc_range_pct(span3, f\"  Span 3 (Nov-Jan): {span3}\")\n    print(f\"  Max %: {max(pct1, pct2, pct3):.2f}\")\n\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
